            {
              "id": "3f71d221-79e7-3e83-a67e-f4f0ff5c2ab9",
              "name": "JWT Token Vulnerability Detected",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe code snippet provided is storing a JSON Web Token (JWT) in the browser's local storage. This is a security vulnerability because local storage is accessible by any script running on the same domain, making it susceptible to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks. If an attacker can run a script on the domain, they can retrieve the JWT and use it to impersonate the user.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid storing sensitive information, such as JWTs, in local storage. Instead, consider using HTTP-only cookies to store JWTs. HTTP-only cookies are not accessible via JavaScript, which makes them immune to XSS attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of using `localStorage.setItem()`, you can set the JWT as an HTTP-only cookie on the server-side. Here's an example using the `express` and `cookie-parser` libraries in Node.js:\n\n```javascript\nconst express = require('express');\nconst cookieParser = require('cookie-parser');\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(cookieParser());\n\napp.get('/login', (req, res) => {\n  // Authenticate user and generate JWT...\n  const token = 'eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwibmFtZSI6IkpvaG4gRG9lIiwiaWF0IjoxNTE2MjM5MDIyfQ.SflKxwRJSMeKKF2QT4fwpMeJf36POk6yJV_adQssw5c';\n\n  res.cookie('token', token, { httpOnly: true });\n  res.send('Logged in!');\n});\n\napp.listen(3000);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following libraries:\n\n- `express`: A web application framework for Node.js.\n- `cookie-parser`: Middleware for parsing cookies in Express apps.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP JWT Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/JSON_Web_Token_for_Java_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)\n- [CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/352.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-352",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/352.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79",
                  "CWE-352"
                ]
              }
